{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Tzohar.</b> An opening through which light enters; it is from the root of tzohorayim. It was made at the top, as is the rule, and since at the top it was one cubit in length, its width was a sixth of a cubit. The ark was in the shape of a triangle, its top pointed, and so its sides were angled; therefore it would not capsize. The opening was on one side, and one would ascend to it by a ladder. We know that the ark was very large; also possible is that Noah's stature was larger than ours, for the cubit was according to his measure. It is possible that when it was divided into three for height, the lower ones were ten cubits. Some say there were many; the verse took a abbreviated path." "<b>Tachtiyyim.</b> A nominal form. So too שְנִיִם, and so too שלשים. Those who ask why it does not say ושלישיים — do they not see? עינים להם ולא יראו; הלא יראו; סלה; קשת; גנב — all nominal forms. And נגיד, פקיד, חסיד, חכם, נבון — nominal forms, each word according to its pattern and structure. The pattern of שלישים is like נגידים, חסידים, for the one is a third, like חסיד. Or possible is that the yod of שנים serves for itself, and the word שלישים along with it. Perhaps the questioners' minds will be at rest."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {1 "תואר השם rendered as 'a nominal form' in both instances; Ibn Ezra is arguing these are nouns, not adjectives. The concluding phrase אולי תנוח דעת השואלים is rendered literally. The list עינים להם ולא יראו / הלא יראו / סלה / קשת / גנב are biblical words that function as nominal forms despite surface irregularity; left untranslated as Ibn Ezra cites them as proof texts without spelling out his argument."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:38.250779662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}